msgid ""
"# False Color Urban composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite is used to visualise urbanized areas more clearly. "
"Vegetation is visible in shades of green, while urbanized areas are "
"represented by white, grey, or purple. Soils, sand, and minerals are shown "
"in a variety of colors. Snow and ice appear as dark blue, and water as "
"black or blue. Flooded areas are very dark blue and almost black. The "
"composite is useful for detecting wildfires and calderas of volcanoes, as "
"they are displayed in shades of red and yellow.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) and [here.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Valse kleuren stedelijk-composiet\n"
"\n"
"Dit composiet wordt gebruikt om verstedelijkte gebieden duidelijker te "
"visualiseren. Vegetatie is zichtbaar in tinten groen, terwijl "
"verstedelijkte gebieden worden weergegeven in wit, grijs of paars. Bodems, "
"zand en mineralen worden in verschillende kleuren getoond. Sneeuw en ijs "
"verschijnen donkerblauw en water zwart of blauw. Overstroomde gebieden zijn "
"zeer donkerblauw en bijna zwart. Het composiet is nuttig voor het "
"detecteren van bosbranden en caldera's van vulkanen, omdat die in tinten "
"rood en geel worden weergegeven.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Meer info "
"[hier](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) en [hier.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Short wave infrared composite (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Short wave infrared (SWIR) measurements can help scientists estimate how "
"much water is present in plants and soil, as water absorbs SWIR "
"wavelengths. Short wave infrared bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) are also useful for distinguishing between cloud types (water clouds "
"versus ice clouds), snow and ice, all of which appear white in visible "
"light. In this composite vegetation appears in shades of green, soils and "
"built-up areas are in various shades of brown, and water appears black. "
"Newly burned land reflects strongly in SWIR bands, making them valuable for "
"mapping fire damages. Each rock type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kortgolvig infrarood-composiet (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Metingen in kortgolvig infrarood (SWIR) kunnen wetenschappers helpen "
"inschatten hoeveel water er in planten en bodem aanwezig is, omdat water "
"SWIR-golflengten absorbeert. Kortgolvig infrarode banden (een band is een "
"gebied van het elektromagnetische spectrum; een satellietsensor kan de "
"aarde in verschillende banden in beeld brengen) zijn ook nuttig om "
"onderscheid te maken tussen wolkentypes (waterwolken versus ijswolken), "
"sneeuw en ijs, die in zichtbaar licht allemaal wit lijken. In dit composiet "
"verschijnt vegetatie in tinten groen, zijn bodems en bebouwde gebieden in "
"diverse tinten bruin en verschijnt water zwart. Pas verbrande grond "
"reflecteert sterk in SWIR-banden, waardoor deze waardevol zijn voor het in "
"kaart brengen van brandschade. Elk gesteentetype reflecteert kortgolvig "
"infrarood licht anders, waardoor het mogelijk is de geologie in kaart te "
"brengen door het gereflecteerde SWIR-licht te vergelijken.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Meer info "
"[hier.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"

msgid ""
"# Scene classification\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scene classification was developed to distinguish between cloudy pixels, "
"clear pixels and water pixels of Sentinel-2 data and is a result of ESA's "
"Scene classification algorithm. Twelve different classifications are "
"provided including classes of clouds, vegetation, soils/desert, water and "
"snow. It does not constitute a land cover classification map in a strict "
"sense.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."
msgstr ""
"# Scèneclassificatie\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scèneclassificatie is ontwikkeld om onderscheid te maken tussen bewolkte "
"pixels, heldere pixels en waterpixels in Sentinel-2-data en is een "
"resultaat van het scèneclassificatie-algoritme van ESA. Er worden twaalf "
"verschillende classificaties geleverd, waaronder klassen voor wolken, "
"vegetatie, bodems/woestijn, water en sneeuw. Het vormt in strikte zin geen "
"landbedekkingskaart.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Meer info "
"[hier](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."

